From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DwUsbHostDxe: reset the core before programming GUSBCFG

On the BCM2712 core behind the Pi 5 USB-C port, the first core soft reset
completes -- GRSTCTL.CSFTRST clears -- and then GRSTCTL.AHBIDLE never
asserts. The driver spends its whole reset deadline on that bit and
declines the controller, so no EFI_USB2_HC_PROTOCOL is published and
nothing on the port can enumerate:

  DwUsbHostDxe: DWC2 core at 0x1000480000, GSNPSID 0x4F54280A
  DwCoreReset: AHBIDLE Timeout!
  DwCoreReset failed
  DwCoreInit failed
  DwUsbHostDxe: controller reset failed: Time out

The core is demonstrably alive and powered: GSNPSID reads back a valid
Synopsys ID (rev 2.80a) and the soft reset itself retires, neither of
which happens on an unpowered block. The VideoCore firmware is newer than
the rpi-eeprom release that brings the DWC PHY up, and the device tree
node is enabled -- so the usual suspects are all excluded.

What remains is the order of the first two register operations.
dwc2_driver_probe() in Linux runs dwc2_check_core_version(), then
dwc2_core_reset(), then dwc2_get_hwparams(), and its comment states the
reason: "Reset before dwc2_get_hwparams() then it could get power-on real
reset value form registers." GUSBCFG is untouched when that reset runs.

This driver descends from u-boot's dwc_otg_core_init(), which instead sets
GUSBCFG.ULPI_EXT_VBUS_DRV and clears GUSBCFG.TERM_SEL_DL_PULSE first, and
resets afterwards. ULPI_EXT_VBUS_DRV configures a ULPI interface; the
BCM2712 core has a UTMI+ PHY (usb@480000 carries phys = <&usbphy>, a
usb-nop-xceiv), so the bit describes hardware that is not there -- and it
is written over whatever state the boot ROM left, because rpiboot drives
this same core as a gadget before EDK2 runs.

Do what Linux does: reset first, then read GUSBCFG back at its power-on
value and program it. The PHY interface selection still needs a reset to
take effect, so that second reset stays; the count is unchanged at two,
the first has just moved ahead of the first write.

The two DwCoreReset() failure messages are renamed to say which one
failed, since "DwCoreReset failed" and "DwCoreReset 2 failed" no longer
describe their positions.

Upstream-Status: Submittable [with an RPi5 platform port]
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
diff -urN a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
@@ -1520,28 +1520,52 @@
     return EFI_DEVICE_ERROR;
   }
 
-  UsbCfg = MmioRead32 (DwHc->DwUsbBase + GUSBCFG);
-
-  UsbCfg |= DWC2_GUSBCFG_ULPI_EXT_VBUS_DRV;
-  UsbCfg &= ~DWC2_GUSBCFG_TERM_SEL_DL_PULSE;
-
-  MmioWrite32 (DwHc->DwUsbBase + GUSBCFG, UsbCfg);
-
+  //
+  // Reset the core before programming GUSBCFG, not after.
+  //
+  // Linux goes dwc2_check_core_version() -> dwc2_core_reset() ->
+  // dwc2_get_hwparams(), and says why the reset comes first: "Reset before
+  // dwc2_get_hwparams() then it could get power-on real reset value form
+  // registers." Nothing has written GUSBCFG at that point.
+  //
+  // This driver inherited u-boot's order instead, which sets
+  // GUSBCFG.ULPI_EXT_VBUS_DRV -- a ULPI-interface bit -- and only then
+  // resets. The BCM2712 core behind the USB-C port has a UTMI+ PHY
+  // (usb@480000 carries phys = <&usbphy>, a usb-nop-xceiv), so those ULPI
+  // bits describe an interface that is not present, and they are written
+  // over whatever state the boot ROM's rpiboot gadget left in the core.
+  // The reset that follows never reports GRSTCTL.AHBIDLE on this part, and
+  // the driver spends its entire deadline on a bit that does not move.
+  //
+  // Resetting first costs nothing on the boards where the old order worked:
+  // a core leaving soft reset has GUSBCFG at its power-on value, which is
+  // precisely what the writes below then modify.
+  //
   Status = DwCoreReset (DwHc, Timeout);
   if (Status != EFI_SUCCESS) {
-    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "DwCoreReset failed\n"));
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "DwCoreReset (initial) failed\n"));
     return Status;
   }
 
+  UsbCfg = MmioRead32 (DwHc->DwUsbBase + GUSBCFG);
+
+  UsbCfg |= DWC2_GUSBCFG_ULPI_EXT_VBUS_DRV;
+  UsbCfg &= ~DWC2_GUSBCFG_TERM_SEL_DL_PULSE;
+
   UsbCfg &= ~(DWC2_GUSBCFG_ULPI_UTMI_SEL | DWC2_GUSBCFG_PHYIF);
   UsbCfg |= CONFIG_DWC2_PHY_TYPE << DWC2_GUSBCFG_ULPI_UTMI_SEL_OFFSET;
   UsbCfg &= ~DWC2_GUSBCFG_DDRSEL;
 
   MmioWrite32 (DwHc->DwUsbBase + GUSBCFG, UsbCfg);
 
+  //
+  // The PHY interface selection only takes effect across a reset, so the
+  // second one stays where it was. Two resets in total, as before -- the
+  // first has simply moved ahead of the first register write.
+  //
   Status = DwCoreReset (DwHc, Timeout);
   if (Status != EFI_SUCCESS) {
-    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "DwCoreReset 2 failed\n"));
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "DwCoreReset (after PHY select) failed\n"));
     return Status;
   }
 
